# Drama Studio bridge timer — Hostinger client container (U6).
#
# This is the platform DEFINITION (a crontab line), not a registration. It lives
# on the container's persistent volume at
#   /data/.openclaw/scripts/drama-studio-timer.cron
# so it survives `docker compose up -d --force-recreate` (the volume is
# persistent; the container layer is not). The operator installs it by handing
# this file to the container's `node` user crontab — install-timer.sh only
# PRINTS that command, it never runs it:
#   docker exec -u node <container> sh -c 'crontab /data/.openclaw/scripts/drama-studio-timer.cron'
#
# DIRECT SHELL: the command is [/bin/sh, run-timer.sh] with an explicit minimal
# environment. No Claude, no claude-nine, no model, no interactive session, no
# idle/agent event. Restart state: cron re-fires every 2 minutes; the script's
# state lives on /data (persistent HOME), so a reboot/recreate/login keeps it.
#
# Placeholders expanded by install-timer.sh:
#   __SCRIPT_PATH__ -> /data/.openclaw/scripts/run-timer.sh
#   __LOG_PATH__    -> /data/.openclaw/logs/drama-studio-timer.log
#   __HOME__        -> /data          (persistent HOME for the node user)
#   __PATH__        -> container PATH with the persistent npm-global first
#   __STORE_DIR__   -> /data/.drama-studio
__SCHEDULE__ HOME=__HOME__ PATH=__PATH__ DS_PLATFORM=hostinger DS_STATE_DIR=__STORE_DIR__ /bin/sh __SCRIPT_PATH__ >> __LOG_PATH__ 2>&1
